        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ultrasound - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MATERIALS:\nQuartz: natural, low coupling, very stable → frequency references\nPZT (lead zirconate titanate): strong coupling, ceramic, dominant for medical imaging\nPVDF (polyvinylidene fluoride): polymer, flexible, lower coupling, wide bandwidth\nLiNbO₃, LiTaO₃: for high-frequency and wide-bandwidth applications"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-ULTRASOUND.md#014",
      "path": [
        "08-ULTRASOUND.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:acoustics:08-ultrasound, git-history:acoustics:08-ultrasound]",
        "canonical_path": "acoustics/08-ULTRASOUND.md",
        "concepts": "[ultrasound]",
        "current_path": "acoustics/08-ULTRASOUND.md",
        "id": "maxim:acoustics:ultrasound",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "acoustics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ultrasound]",
        "section": "acoustics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ultrasound - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COUPLING COEFFICIENT k:\nk² = electrical energy converted / total mechanical energy stored\nPZT: k ≈ 0.5–0.7 (efficient)\nPVDF: k ≈ 0.1–0.2 (less efficient but wide bandwidth)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-ULTRASOUND.md#015",
      "path": [
        "08-ULTRASOUND.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
